This ascension is notable for a couple of reasons. First, I have probably 
never taken so many turns to ascend a valkyrie. I really didn't keep track 
of how many but I would imagine it was a lot.

Second, Dispater made an entrance after being summoned by Baalzebul. In all 
my years playing nethack I have *never* met Dispater and didn't realize he 
was even a creature in the game.

Third, this is my 2nd ascension in 2 games on the new Washington server for 
the tournament and  I got the birdie award with bells on. Woot!

I started out with a lawful human valkyrie and pretty much did all the 
standard things. A made some dumb moves early on, though. The first dumb 
move was that not being an ASCII player I accidentally attacked a green mold 
with my longsword and corroded it. I had color on but I didn't notice that 
the green F was a bit darker than the lichen. The second mistake I made was 
forcing the door that leads to the lower parts of the mine in minetown and 
angering the guards. I got away, but I couldn't safely go back to minetown 
for a while. The first mistake was easily remedied by converting my 
longsword to a rustproof Excalibur. The second mistake...well, I reached 
mine's end and hit a level teleport that put me a level or two above 
minetown, so I never did liberate the luckstone. I just cleared Sokoban, got 
an amulet of reflection and kept going down.

There was a fairly large bookshop with a lot of scrolls on level 10, where I 
managed to get about 6 identify scrolls. I did get a full id on my 2nd try 
after blessing the scrolls at an altar I found. I then blessed the 
now-identified enchant weapon scrolls and got Excalibur up to +6. I then 
proceeded to Medusa's island and made an ice bridge with a wand of cold to 
get to Medusa's island. Normally I would just tunnel down and come up under 
Medusa but if you don't have to do this then it's a good idea not to do so. 
For one, I wasn't sure how I'd fare if I ran into a minotaur. Also, I had 
not yet genocided anything, including mind flayers.

Sure enough, there was a mind flayer on the level right above the castle, 
close enough to track me. I zapped it with a teleport wand and it went 
safely off to another part of the maze. I had a hard fight at the stairs on 
the castle level, and had to go back up the stairs several times. Luckily, 
there was also a gray dragon wandering around on the upper level. I killed 
him and was lucky; he dropped gray dragon scales, which I donned in lieu of 
my elven mithral coat. An elven cloak I had found allowed me to skirt around 
the castle barracks and I managed to find the wand and get some better 
armor, along with a magic marker. I then went back up to one of the altars 
in the main dungeon to make the first of a few mistakes that would make life 
a bit difficult.

First, after writing lots of scrolls, I was careless and instead of charging 
my magic marker to get another 50 charges I accidentally charged a blank 
scroll and got nothing. So some of my armor was neither fixed nor enchanted. 
Along the way, I also found an intriguing helm that I said "what the heck" 
and donned, which turned out to be a helm of opposite alignment. Good bye to 
all the protection I spent gold to get. I couldn't do much about the empty 
magic marker except look around for a charging scroll. The second problem I 
solved by luckily finding a portal to Ft. Ludios. I finished the quest, then 
cleared Ft. Ludios and got about 53,000 gold - good enough to get my 
protection back and then some. I gave the money to a co-aligned priest on 
level 21. I also manage to get Mjollnir and get it enchanted to +6.

With my AC up to about -31 I started some real dungeon exploration. I tend 
to tell Asmodius and Baalzebul these days that they aren't getting any money 
which leads to a fight. Asmodius wasn't bad, but Baalzebul summoned 
Dispater. Dispater hit reasonably hard and combined with Baalzebul appearing 
and stunning me, this was an annoying fight. I tracked them both to the up 
stairs and threw MJ until Dispater was dead. I then chased Baalzebul up the 
stairs but he managed to disappear. I finished him later when I went back to 
minetown to get the candles and took the long way back (yes I could have 
levelported with the quest reward but I wanted to make sure I had a clear 
way up and down the stairs for when I finally got the amulet. It's a good 
thing I did, because I really would not have wanted to finish Baalzebul 
during the ascension run).

My big concern all this time was that I wasn't going to have enough hp or 
scrolls of remove curse to pull this off. But then I realized that I had a 
magic lamp t hat I had been using as a light source and I used it for one 
final wish, which was for a magic marker. In one of my more daring moves I 
used it to fix all my armor and write some detect gold scrolls while holding 
on to the amulet - which meant I was exposed for about 20-30 turns with 
minimal armor. A gamble, but it paid off - with the quest artifact and -41 
AC I was able to finish off any air elementals or other nasties on the 
elemental planes that threatened me.

And I was blessed similarly by probably the easiest Astral plane level ever. 
I took the right fork to where Pestilence was running around and used my 
wand of death on him. A cockatrice was dead ahead to my right, so I offed 
him and used the corpse. I went straight to the altar, which was the correct 
one. I didn't even need conflict to pull it off.

It was kind of messy, but entertaining nevertheless. 




